From 810154956f0422b8448dc205b296e96a0b5e6f7e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: havok2-htwo <havok2-htwo@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 19:46:31 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] engine: pipelined solo decode beside --batch slots
 (opt-in STRATA_SOLO_PIPELINE=1)

With --batch, a request the server sends to the solo path (GEN) can run the
pipelined decode loop (--pipeline-windows 2: two verifiers per stage, windows
overlapped across the stages) instead of the serial solo loop.  Batch windows,
admissions (BGEN's first token, incl. STRATA_ADMIT_MERGE_FIRST) and all prompt
reads keep their serial windows.

- gate: STRATA_SOLO_PIPELINE=1 lifts "not with --batch slots" for
  --pipeline-windows 2 (auto -> 2 when --batch is on); refused with --batch-mtp.
- the even verifiers stay the batch/serial ones: no set_always_publish; only
  their stream is the stage's shared one.  Verifier::set_pl_mode gives their
  pipelined windows own graphs (exec_pl_: publish every row, no one-token
  self-commit); a T>=2 window of an all-resident stage shares its zero-doorbell
  exec_ (identical recording).  Toggled on after the gate, off after pl_drain.
- odd verifiers (ver_b) sized like the even ones (max_t 8) so both parities run
  the serial loop's window shapes; capture_all(up_to = --spec).
- VRAM: a later front stage also holds its GDN snapshots out of its cache; a
  boot pre-check per card (verifier + snapshots + kVramSafeMib + 256 MiB) keeps
  the solo path serial instead of loaning/paging; per-card cost of the second
  verifiers/snapshots and of the first capture is logged.
- a solo request stays serial (said once): images in context, batch slots
  active, groups in flight, an all-resident stage out of VRAM, snapshot size
  changed, penalties/coupled drafts (as before).
- rules in include/strata/program/solo_pipeline.hpp, test solo_pipeline_test.
Off (default): kernels SASS-identical, host default branches unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
